{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"GATE EVIDENCE (recorded up front, since this proof is external to the repo — the lesson from dc0d's blocked close).\n\nCommit b17f4989f, Gerrit change 1032 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1032), stacked on 1023->1014->1012.\n\nSIZE — the point of the task: runner.py 800 -> 655 LOC (criterion: under 700, real headroom rather than sitting on the 800 gate). structured_run.py 178 LOC (criterion: >=100 anti-fragmentation floor, <500 target ceiling). Both inside AGENTS.md's 200-500 target band.\n\nLEAF RULE: structured_run.py imports runner ONLY under TYPE_CHECKING (line 27, for the RunRequest annotation). Verified this guard is load-bearing, not stylistic — mutating it into a runtime import fails 3 tests with 'ImportError: cannot import name RunRequest from partially initialized module', i.e. a genuine circular import.\n\nBEHAVIOUR PRESERVATION — the strongest evidence available for a relocation: ZERO test-logic edits, and in fact zero test-file edits at all. runner.py imports the moved callables BY NAME, so they remain bound in its namespace and all seven reference sites keep resolving untouched: four LSP-resolvable import sites (test_pydantic_ai_runner.py:18, test_agent_build_invariants.py:20, test_llm_failure_matrix.py:71, workflow/test_plan_review_verify_recovery.py:22) and — the risky class — three string-literal monkeypatch targets (test_pydantic_ai_runner.py:382 and :425, test_execution_mode_dispatch.py) that patch runner_mod._pai_structured by string. Had the implementation referenced structured_run._pai_structured instead, those patches would have silently stopped taking effect rather than failing loudly. All 91 tests across those five files pass unchanged.\n\nFULL GATING SUITE: 7524 passed, 29 skipped, 114 deselected, exit 0, 27m14s — exactly the 7517 baseline plus the 7 new seam tests, no regressions. make lint: 'All checks passed!' + '1297 files already formatted'. make typecheck: clean.\n\nDEPENDENCY ENUMERATION: done by walking each cluster member's AST and intersecting free names against runner.py's module-level names, AFTER a hand-written grep produced an incomplete list (it missed usage_log). Both sweeps required by the plan were run: the symbol-reference query for import sites AND the string-literal grep for monkeypatch targets, which an LSP structurally cannot resolve — that exact class broke stories 7468 and f184 earlier in this epic."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785397426059254001,"uuid":"ea8e510a-af26-435b-ac0e-cb30097f854f"}